From 133fb7a5c17f4699e8cc41526577890e7feff799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 17:54:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): wire Facebook Login end-to-end (backend endpoint
 + Flutter session manager)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backend (FastAPI):
- New FacebookAuthRequest model with access_token: str.
- New POST /api/auth/facebook endpoint that:
    1. Verifies the user-supplied access_token via Facebook's
       https://graph.facebook.com/debug_token endpoint, using
       APP_ID|APP_SECRET as the app access token. Confirms the token
       is valid AND was minted for OUR Facebook app (defense against
       cross-app token replay).
    2. Fetches /me?fields=id,email,name with the validated token.
    3. Find-or-creates the user keyed on email (mirrors /auth/google).
       New users get the same initial credit allocation as Google
       sign-ups (auth_provider = 'facebook', facebook_id stored for
       future linking).
    4. Returns the standard TokenResponse with a Legacy Table session
       JWT, so the rest of the app treats the session identically to
       Google/Apple sign-ins.
- Requires two env vars (Doc to set in Railway):
    FACEBOOK_APP_ID      — 898895229882962 (public)
    FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET  — set in Railway only, NEVER committed
- Returns 400 if Facebook doesn't surface an email (FB lets users hide
  it). Matches existing Apple flow which has the same requirement.

Mobile (Flutter):
- api_config.dart: add facebookAuth endpoint path constant.
- auth_service.dart: new facebookSignIn(accessToken) method mirroring
  googleSignIn / appleSignIn.
- session_manager.dart: new facebookLogin(accessToken) that calls
  AuthService.facebookSignIn, persists the session token, identifies
  the user with RevenueCat, and returns isNewlyCreatedUser (so the
  caller can route new users to /subscription).
- login_screen.dart: _handleFacebookSignIn now calls
  sessionManager.facebookLogin instead of just showing a placeholder
  snackbar. New Facebook users land on /subscription, returning users
  on /home — same routing as Google.

End-to-end on iOS after this lands + Railway env vars set:
  Tap Continue with Facebook → Meta SDK dialog → I agree
    → backend verifies token → user found/created
    → returned to /home (or /subscription for new accounts)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
